id: pm-memory-higm
title: Apply Fleet CI v2 and bound release-gate test lifecycles
description: "Companion pm-cli-website-dyhg. Replace duplicated hosted PR release gates with hosted quick checks and exhaustive scheduled/main deep gates. Preserve required test (22), test (26), codeql and unchanged 100% coverage thresholds. Fix detached CLI fixture teardown writers tracked by issue #75; fail hanging test files with a hard watchdog. Full depth preserves all original seeds and assertions."
type: Task
pm_format_version: 2
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[5]: ci,"gh:unbraind/pm-memory#75","gh:unbraind/pm-memory#76",performance,tests
created_at: "2026-11-04T03:26:26.179Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-15T19:04:00.453Z"
author: orchestrator
acceptance_criteria: Hosted quick required checks complete within 15 minutes including queueing; full default and deep mode retain all original seed receipts and release checks; CLI delayed-writer isolation regression and file-watchdog regression pass; quick coverage remains 100 percent in every dimension; record local and PR measurements; leave this Task open for owner verification
comments[41]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-15T03:42:01.837Z",codex-sol,"Applying Fleet CI v2; companion pm-cli-website-dyhg. Reusing this existing CI/performance Task. Required checks confirmed: test (22), test (26), codeql. CodeQL stays unfiltered because it is required. Plan: hosted quick PR gates, exhaustive four-combination local deep tier, deterministic depth prefixes with unchanged 100% coverage, bounded test lifecycle and issue #75 regression, then measured PR checks. Release workflow and release verifiers are out of scope."
  "2026-11-15T03:48:18.439Z",codex-sol,"Baseline run 43627397337: full gate steps Node 22 npm 182m51s, Node 26 npm 56m33s, Node 26 Bun 41m08s. Current main has three runtime legs, so deep restores the requested Node 22 Bun combination as well. The pinned CLI dispatches detached telemetry flush children; replacement diagnostic environments drop test suppression. Child test environments now explicitly disable telemetry. An independent probe confirmed Node --test-timeout does not terminate an idle file after its last passing test, so an unreferenced per-file failure watchdog is required. No coverage thresholds or source scope changed."
  "2026-11-15T03:50:36.924Z",codex-sol,"Recovered baseline test timings from the successful main Node 26 job log: model 1302.75s, forward-only update boundary sweep 544.59s, owned state 441.94s, 220-source round trip 395.36s, grammar 365.66s. The canceled run 43616440465 last emitted test 346 and retained model/coverage children, so its logs do not prove all tests finished. Explicit watchdog regression now fails an idle file after a passing test. The real-CLI probe demonstrates unsuppressed detached telemetry dispatch and zero dispatch with isolated child settings; diagnostic assertions and cleanup failures remain load-bearing."
  "2026-11-15T03:51:58.733Z",codex-sol,"Validation harness correction: the first linked quick-coverage invocation hit pm test default 120-second limit; this was a harness timeout, not a suite failure. The linked command now has a 2700-second bound. Expanded depth selection to the heavy seeded forward-boundary schedules using the same deterministic prefix and retained the full boundary enumeration in deep mode. The 220-source size-contract test keeps every row but disables unrelated Git discovery, matching existing non-Git fixture practice."
  "2026-11-15T03:55:59.372Z",codex-sol,"Additional lifecycle fix: the independent native peer used a replacement environment and fire-and-forget child.kill teardown. It now gets explicit telemetry suppression and is registered as an owned fixture child; fixture cleanup awaits process/stdio close before removing the root, with bounded SIGKILL escalation. A controlled child writes lock files during delayed shutdown; the regression proves shutdown completes before root removal. Focused initial suite passed 67/67; Node 22 workflow/lifecycle smoke passed 5/5. Strict YAML parsing passed (actionlint unavailable). Typecheck, lint and zero-duplication passed; generated changelog is consistent."
  "2026-11-15T03:59:14.301Z",codex-sol,"Preserved the packed-documentation allowlist test in test/shipped-files.acceptance.ts and added it to test:install, so the Node 22 PR unit suite performs no npm pack operation. Removed speed-dependent per-test deadlines from finite seeded corpus workers; the independently tested per-file watchdog now bounds them, including idle handles and teardown, with deep slow-host scaling. No successful test process is force-exited."
  "2026-11-15T04:04:44.277Z",codex-sol,"Slow-host validation exposed the requested timing issue: two scanner properties exceeded the unchanged 500ms baseline during concurrent local work (66/68 passed). Local proof now explicitly uses PM_TEST_TIME_SCALE=3, matching deep settings and preserving the baseline on hosted quick jobs. Superseded the unscaled coverage run after this evidence and final watchdog/lifecycle edits; rerunning final code with scaled bounds. The hard watchdog passes both idle-handle and blocked-event-loop regressions on Node 22 and Node 26; final lifecycle suite passes 6/6 on both."
  "2026-11-15T04:12:09.425Z",codex-sol,"Preflight audit found zero production vulnerabilities and publish-attestation verification passed. Local strict health initially detected an unrelated global pm-github/locked-CLI version skew; using a disposable global PM context matching a fresh CI runner avoids that ambient extension collision. No global extension, repository variable, protection rule or release verifier was changed. Full-depth local coverage is not planned: the baseline hosted Node 26 gate already needed 56m33s and this shared host is slower; deep must certify full depth after merge, and the old 182m51s Node 22 gate remains a timeout risk until measured with these changes."
  "2026-11-15T04:14:09.792Z",codex-sol,"Final scaled touched-test command passed: PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick PM_TEST_TIME_SCALE=3 node --import ./test/support/file-deadline.ts --test --test-concurrency=2 test/ci-lifecycle.test.ts test/release-ci.test.ts test/property-seeds.test.ts test/review-round4.test.ts test/review-r1.test.ts test/review-r11.test.ts test/source-safety.test.ts test/worker-budget.test.ts. Linked runner measured 244.103s (247.22s including wrapper). Strict health passes in a fresh global PM context, matching CI. Workflow/lifecycle smoke passes 8/8, shipped-doc acceptance 1/1, zero duplication and strict YAML validation pass. The complete quick coverage and release gates remain pending."
  "2026-11-15T04:15:35.465Z",codex-sol,"Refined full-depth measurement from main run 43627397337: the Node 26 coverage suite itself took 3208835.746ms (53m28.84s), with 893 tests and 39 measured sources meeting every threshold. This directly exceeds the roughly 45-minute condition for attempting full coverage locally, independently of the later audit/pack/acceptance steps. Full-depth verification remains assigned to ci-deep after merge."
  "2026-11-15T04:27:59.528Z",codex-sol,"Current standalone quick coverage has completed the owned-state property prefix: all 50 sequences passed in 391.978s. This is a local shared-host measurement, not directly comparable to hosted full depth or PR queue-inclusive time. Increased the stored local quick-coverage timeout to 7200s for future invocations; the current invocation retains its original 2700s deadline. No test or workflow timeout was raised by this metadata change."
  "2026-11-15T04:42:07.545Z",codex-sol,"The local Bun graph smoke (bun install --no-save) passed in 4.36 seconds. Required contexts rechecked live: test (22), test (26), codeql; CodeQL path exclusions remain intentionally absent. Standalone quick coverage is still running without reported failures on the shared host; the future linked coverage timeout is 7200 seconds, while this already-running invocation retains its original 2700-second harness limit."
  "2026-11-15T04:45:02.351Z",codex-sol,Final fixed-count audit also applies testDepth to the 512-case enumerated quote/escape corpus. Quick uses 52 seeds plus all fixed spelling fixtures; the original complete verdict digest was reverified before freezing the selected prefix digest. Deep retains the original full digest. The 220-source test remains complete because its size is the contract.
  "2026-11-15T04:46:37.949Z",codex-sol,"Both quoted-scanner parity runs passed: PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick node --import ./test/support/file-deadline.ts --test --test-name-pattern=\"quoted scanner\" test/sdk-review-r8.test.ts (1/1), and the same command at PM_TEST_DEPTH=full (1/1). The full verdict digest is unchanged. This targeted full corpus check is not full-depth suite certification."
  "2026-11-15T04:52:16.658Z",codex-sol,"The standalone quick coverage command was terminated by the outer pm harness at 2700.062 seconds (SIGTERM), with no assertion failures reported before termination. This is incomplete evidence, not a coverage pass; any partial report is invalid. The complete quick release:check will now rerun coverage under the corrected 7200-second linked-test harness, then execute audit, pack, changelog, attestation and real packed npm/Bun acceptance."
  "2026-11-15T05:07:54.541Z",codex-sol,"The final remaining large-count seeded loop was the packet-budget property (300 generated sets), now depth-selected to the same first 30 sets. The in-flight release gate was deliberately superseded before completion so final local validation uses this exact test configuration. The remaining fixed large fixtures are product size/complexity contracts or complete seed-ledger guards, rather than sampled seed loops. No result from a stopped run is claimed as a pass."
  "2026-11-15T05:09:01.401Z",codex-sol,"Final prefix validation passed in 20.632 seconds: packet-budget and quoted-scanner tests at both quick and full depth. Typecheck and lint passed after the final packet-budget helper change. Restarting the complete quick release gate on the final selected-seed configuration; the earlier superseded release invocation is excluded from success evidence."
  "2026-11-15T05:51:30.920Z",codex-sol,"Live diagnosis during final quick release validation: apparent output pause at 345 reported passes was finite work, not an idle process. Model workers advanced to batches starting at 20, 25, 30 and 35 of the selected 50 sequences; the environment confirms quick depth and time scale 3. The sibling lossless suite was also active. This reinforces the distinction between unfinished model work in canceled hosted logs and the separately demonstrated detached telemetry/teardown defect."
  "2026-11-15T06:10:13.711Z",codex-sol,"Final quick model validation completed all 50 sequences and 2290 SDK-read steps in 1326.501 seconds on the shared local host; the final two batches were observed advancing at starts 40 and 45 before completion. Fresh-tracker field/adapter export law also passed in 675.220 seconds locally versus 81.448 seconds in the hosted baseline, illustrating why local and hosted timings must be labeled separately. The complete release gate is still running without reported failures; no overall pass or coverage percentage is claimed yet."
  "2026-11-15T06:23:49.737Z",codex-sol,"Deep schedule refined to 00:53 UTC: its nominal 120-minute execution window ends at 02:53, thirty minutes before the 03:23 release cron. This supersedes the earlier 02:53 start decision. Queue delays can still shift actual execution; the per-ref concurrency and hard timeout remain unchanged. Product tests and coverage configuration are unchanged by this scheduling edit."
  "2026-11-15T06:31:09.734Z",codex-sol,"Complete quick validation found one stale tooling assertion and exactly one uncovered source branch. Result: 896/897 tests passed; coverage statements/functions/lines 100%, branches 99.97%. The assertion still required a standalone identity step, although identity remains first in the Node 26 release gate. The uncovered core.ts branch rejects invalid quote spans ending in a backslash, previously reached only by late quote-corpus seeds. Added deterministic benign-tail and later-credential refusal cases at both depths; thresholds and source inventory remain unchanged. This failed attempt is not counted as successful release proof."
  "2026-11-15T06:34:30.607Z",codex-sol,"The deterministic malformed quote-tail regression records four hits on the previously uncovered core.ts:189 branch in diagnostic c8 coverage. Corrected identity-gate wiring and quote-tail tests pass at both quick and full depth via linked test 6 (3.567 seconds). Typecheck and lint pass. Separate audit, pack dry-run, changelog and attestation checks pass; packed acceptance is still running before the complete gate restart."
  "2026-11-15T06:38:18.296Z",codex-sol,"Separate release tail passed: production audit, pack dry-run, changelog consistency, publish attestation verifier and all four packed acceptance tests (npm/npx, Bun/bunx, reference-suffix refusal parity and shipped documentation). Total local wall time 326.78 seconds; acceptance runner 320.495 seconds. The complete quick release gate is now restarted with the deterministic missing-branch regression and corrected CI identity assertion, both already passing targeted validation."
  "2026-11-15T07:54:43.744Z",codex-sol,"Final code c65d2b1: the linked quick release:check passed end-to-end (exit 0), 4354.938s inside the tracker runner / 4356.33s process wall time. Coverage passed 898/898 tests in 3399.967s with exact 100% statements, branches, functions and lines for all 39 authored sources. Packed npm/npx and Bun/bunx acceptance passed 4/4 in 897.376s. Identity, typecheck, lint, zero-duplication, build, docstring, audit, pack, changelog and publish attestation gates all passed. Targeted lifecycle/workflow/seed regressions and strict YAML parse passed; Bun install smoke passed in 4.36s. Full-depth coverage was not repeated locally: quick coverage alone takes 56m40s here, beyond the roughly 45-minute allowance. Full certification remains CI Deep after merge. Next: publish and measure every protected check from the jobs API."
  "2026-11-15T07:55:20.056Z",codex-sol,"Published PR #76 (https://github.com/unbraind/pm-memory/pull/76), initial head 8729cdd, after the shared dispatch hold expired. Exact published body verified against the prepared body, with Fixes #75, main tracker link, full tier inventory and local proof. Protected check names remain test (22), test (26), codeql; CodeQL path filters deliberately omitted because it is protected. Awaiting jobs-API queue/execution/wall measurements before final receipt."
  "2026-11-15T08:13:05.447Z",codex-sol,"Initial hosted Node 26 passed at head 8729cdd: job wall 16m11s, queue 2s; release gate 15m55s. Coverage took 832.562s and packed acceptance 110.037s. Largest test: the fixed 220-source contract 231.64s, then model prefix 97.42s. Node 22 remains running. This exceeds the requested 15-minute target. Node sorts test files, preventing a heavy-first argument order; the runner still serializes independent files into only two lanes. Raising file concurrency to four while retaining the existing shared model-worker slot cap, all seed counts and every assertion; will rerun validation and hosted measurements."
  "2026-11-15T08:14:36.533Z",codex-sol,"Four-file scheduling targeted validation passed 60/60 in 22.612s (ci-lifecycle, release-ci, tooling, worker-budget), plus typecheck, lint and changelog consistency. Only the independent unit-file concurrency changes from two to four; packed acceptance retains two and the shared model-worker cap is unchanged. Repeating the complete local quick release gate with the final configuration. Initial hosted Node 22 is still executing; a superseding push will cancel it, so it is explicitly missing evidence rather than approval."
  "2026-11-15T08:33:54.826Z",codex-sol,"The four-file coverage experiment exceeded the earlier 16m13s hosted pass, so coverage returns to two file slots; Node 22 npm test retains four. Stopped the owned superseded local gate; no passing result is claimed for that attempt. The largest fixed contract is adapted by payload shape: quick uses 25 sources × 32 KiB, full keeps the original 220 × 4 KiB. Both still require a manifest larger than 1 MiB and verify every restored body through both real harnesses. This keeps the original many-source contract in CI Deep while avoiding hundreds of repeated SDK publications in every PR. Running its targeted quick check before repeating complete validation."
  "2026-11-15T08:36:46.402Z",codex-sol,"Revised quick aggregate test passed: 25 × 32 KiB sources, both harnesses and >1 MiB manifest, 142.552s test / 143.802s runner versus 891.261s for the previous local 220-source quick test. Full keeps exactly 220 × 4 KiB. Static gates passed with zero duplication. Restoring both unit and coverage file concurrency to the original two: the four-file hosted attempt is slower and is not accepted as evidence. Next hosted head isolates this inventory-shape improvement; the complete local quick release gate will be rerun from that head."
  "2026-11-15T08:40:10.324Z",codex-sol,"Downloaded superseded four-file logs: Node 26 fixed inventory increased from 231.64s to 337.38s and model from 97.42s to 252.34s; Node 22 forward-boundary file hit the explicit 600s deadline. Four-file scheduling was therefore reverted in both unit and coverage runners. Node 22 compile-cache cold/warm SDK startup probe showed no repeatable gain (uncached 0.60-1.17s, warm 0.92-1.27s); cache not introduced, preserving precise coverage behavior. Third hosted head 3d5e6b4 isolates the smaller quick inventory with original scheduling. Repeating complete local release proof now."
  "2026-11-15T09:21:27.021Z",codex-sol,"Root cause of Node 22 throughput: Store allocated two AsyncLocalStorage engines per instance; Node 22 retains enabled engines until disable(), causing per-async-operation work to grow. Reproduction: 500 enabled engines increased a 5000-await loop from 2.85ms to 962.17ms on Node 22, while Node 26 stayed 1.24ms. New Store shares one engine with per-instance/per-binding symbol scopes; contexts are not disabled at write exit, preserving stale detached-writer refusal. The allocation regression rejects prior source (52 engines versus warmed 2), and new nested-scope/Node 22 tests passed. A real 5-sequence model control previously hit 240s; with the fix it passed in 65.39s. The third hosted Node 22 job reached its 30-minute timeout (no pass); Node 26 passed 14m38s, 898 tests and all 39 coverage sources. Also fixed a relative watchdog import inherited by the cwd-changing SDK lease fork, and made that fixture child owned through close. Rechecking stale-writer and cross-scope behavior before publication."
  "2026-11-15T09:24:24.991Z",codex-sol,"Final targeted context/lifecycle/fence suite passed 15/15 on Node 22 (8.485s) and Node 26 (6.127s), including detached stale publication refusal, expired-writer item/file/export refusal, nested Store scope restoration and bounded context-engine reuse. The same linked test passed through pm test index 8. Typecheck, lint, zero duplication, docstring and changelog checks passed. The temporary unread-pipe hypothesis was discarded; fork cancellation was caused by a relative inherited watchdog import after cwd changed, fixed with an absolute module URL. Source and tests are ready for the complete quick gate and new hosted measurements."
  "2026-11-15T13:42:44.336Z",codex-sol,"Review round: preserve cheap-path privacy and identity checks where applicable, restore portable test behavior, and verify generated-case assertions. Run targeted gates and required revert proofs; leave review threads untouched and wait for the dispatch hold before pushing."
  "2026-11-15T13:48:53.747Z",codex-sol,"Review findings PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc63o98b and PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc63o98h fixed. Linked gates passed: typecheck, build, test compilation, lint, 52 targeted lifecycle/workflow/tooling tests, strict unique-key YAML, changelog and identity checks. Missing-bash control: local skips with exit 0; CI=true fails with exit 1. Scale 1.1 regression passes with integer ceiling; a scratch copy reverting the ceiling fails (111.10000000000001 versus 112). No measured coverage sources changed; package coverage was not run."
  "2026-11-15T14:24:11.895Z",codex-sol,"Round 2: fixing the supplied review findings, auditing the whole CI v2 diff for the same defect classes, and running the requested focused gates. Review threads remain untouched."
  "2026-11-15T14:32:27.090Z",codex-sol,"Round 2 complete: only the newline-filename fixture is conditional on non-win32; every portable routing case and the rename/deletion case still run on Windows. Audited the CI v2 filename fixtures for other newly introduced forbidden filename controls. Validation passed: typecheck, lint, 52 workflow/lifecycle/tooling tests, a fresh 2-test routing run through pm test --run --only-last --progress, and strict parsing of every workflow YAML file. Native Windows execution remains CI evidence, not a local claim."
  "2026-11-15T14:33:49.777Z",codex-sol,"Additional health probe is not green: strict health reports pm-github extension-host version skew; tracked separately as pm-memory-ci-health-skew, with stale in-progress items advisory. No dependencies or extension installation state changed. Requested gates remain passing; fresh Windows and CI health are unverified."
  "2026-11-15T18:50:27.040Z",codex-sol,"Round C: verify the supplied review findings, repair failing checks, audit CI tier boundaries and harness controls, and run focused gates. Review threads remain untouched; no merge or closure."
  "2026-11-15T18:57:54.662Z",codex-sol,"Writer-wait finding is valid: mock-clock advance uses the same harness scale as the deadline, tested at 0.5, 1 and 3. Self-review rejects invalid timer scales and validates worker scale before spawn. Product writer waits remain unchanged. Self-review checks documentation/privacy/identity gates, unscaled product budgets, integer timeouts, validation before spawn, platform filenames and generated-only quick thresholds."
  "2026-11-15T18:59:30.735Z",codex-sol,"Self-review additionally restores input-sensitive docs-path gates: identity/privacy, packaging and attestation validation, plus applicable docs/tooling tests. These cheap-path requirements are in the rollout template. New failure-injection tests execute each documentation block."
  "2026-11-15T19:03:59.616Z",codex-sol,"Round C validation passed: typecheck, test TypeScript compilation, focused behavior and workflow/tooling suites, strict unique-key YAML parsing, and package changelog regeneration/check. Lint passed where the package provides a lint script; packages without one passed their existing docstring gate. No configured coverage source changed, so no package coverage run was added. Existing isolated coverage-tooling fixtures are part of the focused tooling suites. All supplied review findings are valid and repaired. Self-review additionally preserves executable tracker scans and all applicable docs/privacy/identity/package/attestation gates. Product budgets and coverage thresholds remain unchanged. Validation uses the local Node 24 runtime; Node 22/26, native Windows and deep runtime certification remain CI evidence. Threads untouched; no merge or item closure. Release ownership after recording this evidence. The initial combined batch had 104 passing tests and one obsolete workflow expectation after expanding the docs block; that expectation was corrected, and the focused release-CI plus docs/lifecycle rerun passed. Semantic and worker behavior passed in the combined batch."
